the-firm-as-one-program-80 = unlines (cons "- **S4** What Hayek argued prices must carry becomes directly available, so prices stop being the main way the economy coordinates ([S3: Prices converge on what is true, so the edge that profits came from shrinks ([S2])], [P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  Hayek argued in 1945 that no central planner could hold the knowledge dispersed across a society, so prices had to carry it in compressed form. Hyperactivity is not a central planner: it has no canonical state, every participant holds its own, and constructions are exchanged between peers. But the knowledge that prices compress becomes available directly, with its evidence, to every participant. Once that holds, prices stop being the primary carrier of coordination, and an economy built around competing partial knowledge gives way to one built around shared knowledge. The trading firm is where this starts, because no institution has more money riding on the gap between what prices know and what is true. The same mechanism, aimed at knowledge instead of money, is the dispelling of ignorance across the human superorganism: thousands of minds in one firm becoming one reasoning process is the small case of billions of minds doing the same." nil))
